@title Ferry Ticketing Platform
@subtitle Tidewater Ferries online ticketing on Azure, region North Europe
@author Digital Channels, Owner
@date 2026-09-22

## Overview
Passengers book through Azure Front Door, and every booking is written to one database.
Each booking is also announced as an event so that the scanners at the terminals stay in step.

## Diagram
diagram tix dir=TB title="Ticketing platform"
tix: pax "Passengers" user
tix: fd "Front Door" lb
tix: web "Booking Web App" svc
tix: api "Ticketing API" svc focus
tix: db "Reservations DB" db "Azure SQL" focus
tix: bus "Booking Events" queue "Service Bus"
tix: scan "Port Terminal Scanners" ext
tix: pay "Payment Provider" ext
tix: pax -> fd : HTTPS
tix: fd -> web : origin request
tix: web -> api : REST
tix: api -> db : SQL, port 1433
tix: api -> pay : card authorization
tix: api -> bus : ticket issued
tix: bus --> scan : sync every 30 s
tix: group app "App subnet 10.50.1.0/24" web, api
tix: group data "Data subnet 10.50.2.0/24" db, bus
tix: group vnet "Ticketing VNet 10.50.0.0/16" app, data
tix: group sub "Ticketing subscription" vnet
tix: legend

## Capacity
table = Component,Capacity; Booking Web App,"3 to 10 instances, scales at 60% CPU"; Ticketing API,4 to 16 pods; Reservations DB,"8 vCores, read replica in the paired region"

## Recovery targets
kpi Recovery point objective | 5 min
kpi Recovery time objective | 1 h
kpi Last tested | 2026-08-19
